@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+# PQ46 stock cruise trim candidate
+
+This branch contains an application-layer prototype for changing the stock PQ cruise setpoint through `GRA_Neu` short button presses. It does not send throttle, brake, ABS, or `ACC_System` acceleration commands.
+
+The candidate is disabled when `/data/pq46/stock_cruise_mode` is missing. The mode is read when `CarController` starts, so changing it requires restarting openpilot.
+
+| File value | Mode | CAN behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `0` or missing | Off | No additional button messages |
+| `1` | Observe | Calculates and logs a temporary lead target; sends nothing |
+| `2` | Manual test | Consumes one `up` or `down` test command and waits for setpoint acknowledgement |
+| `3` | Lead trim | May send one short up/down press at a time after lead confirmation |
+
+Create the mode file without using the compiled Params registry:
+
+```sh
+mkdir -p /data/pq46
+echo -n 1 > /data/pq46/stock_cruise_mode
+```
+
+In manual test mode, queue exactly one command:
+
+```sh
+echo -n down > /data/pq46/stock_cruise_test_command
+```
+
+The command file is deleted as soon as it is read. A command is sent only while openpilot and the stock cruise are engaged and a nonzero stock setpoint is available. The controller then waits for `cruiseState.speed` to move by at least 0.5 km/h in the requested direction. A 1.5 second timeout latches a fault for the rest of that cruise session.
+
+Lead-trim defaults:
+
+- model probability at least 0.70;
+- lateral lead position within 1.8 m of path center;
+- slower closing lead confirmed for 1.0 second;
+- desired time gap 2.0 seconds plus a five-second closing-speed buffer;
+- temporary target no lower than 55 km/h;
+- lead loss confirmed for 2.0 seconds before restoring the saved driver ceiling;
+- at least 0.5 seconds between button presses;
+- every press requires stock setpoint acknowledgement.
+
+Physical cruise-button activity cancels pending virtual commands and takes priority. Brake, accelerator, loss of engagement, missing stock setpoint, or acknowledgement failure prevents additional automatic presses.
+
+## Required vehicle validation
+
+Do not enable mode 3 before confirming all of the following in modes 1 and 2:
+
+1. `GRA_Neu` is transmitted on the expected external bus and the Panda firmware permits it.
+2. One `GRA_Down_kurz`/`GRA_Up_kurz` frame is recognized as one short press.
+3. The actual speed increment for each signal is known.
+4. `ACC_GRA_Anzeige.ACA_V_Wunsch` reports the stock cruise target and acknowledges virtual presses.
+5. Injected button frames do not appear as physical stalk input on the receive path.
+
+The candidate deliberately stops if the vehicle does not expose a usable setpoint acknowledgement. It does not estimate success by counting transmitted presses.
